   "nota": "Auditor rotation: under CVM Resolution No. 23/2021, art. 31, the same independent auditor may not serve the same client for more than five consecutive fiscal years, with a minimum interval of three fiscal years before being hired again; under art. 31-A, the term is up to ten consecutive fiscal years when the company has a statutory audit committee in permanent operation and the auditor is a firm. The Resolution has been in force since 2021-04-01 (art. 41); before that, the equivalent rule was in arts. 31 and 31-A of CVM Instruction No. 308/1999, revoked by the Resolution (art. 40, I). A change of auditor is a fact, not an alert.",
